domain ADR0036:
  description "ADR-0036 revision 1: draft test evidence follows draft Causes. Status Accepted."

problem P1:
  |
    ADR-0034 defines source-matched, Cause-linked, non-stale test evidence but does
    not specify the evidence status when the verification Seal or a required Cause
    is draft. The current selector labels such tests active/current and includes
    their results in the authoritative aggregate.

evidence E1:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0034 revision 1 lists a verification REF, exact source binding,
    matching workfile bytes, explicit governing Cause Links, and a non-stale
    required chain. It does not mention draft status.

evidence E2:
  |
    On 2026-09-16 scripts/test-authority.mjs did not inspect the draft flag. Two
    of its five active unit tests had draft verification Seals. This is a local
    observation, not a claim about future inventory counts.

evidence E3:
  |
    SealGraph defines draft as explicit provisional sealing. Its normal
    non-draft publication requires every direct and reachable Cause target to
    be a non-draft active revision leaf. A source match and absence of stale
    paths do not by themselves remove provisional status.

evidence OWNER_DIRECTION:
  |
    On 2026-09-16 the product owner stated that test results based on draft
    grounds are themselves draft, then instructed creation of an ADR that
    clarifies ADR-0034 draft treatment. This directs the subject of this
    proposal but is not acceptance of this exact ADR revision.

premise AUTHORITY_DIRECTION:
  |
    A selector and a passing test provide downstream evidence only. Neither can
    establish acceptance or finality of a draft governing Cause.

premise SCOPE:
  |
    This decision concerns the status and authoritative aggregation of
    repository test results. It does not judge whether tested behavior is
    correct, amend source requirements, accept draft authority artifacts,
    require wholesale resealing, or authorize implementation or release.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Keep draft-backed results labeled current; exclude draft-backed tests from
    authoritative selection while permitting explicitly labeled diagnostic
    execution; or add a new normal suite state that executes draft tests but
    separately aggregates provisional outcomes. The middle option is the
    smallest change that prevents provisional results from being reported as
    final without adding a new aggregate execution contract.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E3, OWNER_DIRECTION, AUTHORITY_DIRECTION:
  |
    Propose that a test result is draft evidence when its verification Seal is
    draft or any required direct or transitive Cause Seal is draft. Source match
    and non-staleness do not promote that result to final current evidence.

decision D2 based_on D1, E2, OPTIONS, SCOPE:
  |
    Propose that the authoritative selector report such a test as provisional
    with reason draft_basis and exclude it from the authoritative pass/fail
    aggregate. It may still be run by an explicit diagnostic command, whose
    pass or fail is reported as draft evidence for the exact recorded basis.
    This decision does not require a new diagnostic command or UI.

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, E1, AUTHORITY_DIRECTION:
  |
    Propose that ADR-0034 missing-Seal, wrong-source, changed-source, missing-
    Cause, and stale conditions retain their existing disabled treatment. A
    stale or otherwise invalid chain is not made usable by labeling it draft.
    Immutable historical Seals remain evidence only for their exact original
    grounds. A later non-draft result needs a reviewed new verification Seal
    against the applicable non-draft current Cause chain; no automatic promotion.

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-17, after exact ADR-0036 revision 1 and its complete Japanese
    review scope were presented, the product owner replied "はい。受け入れます。"
    to the question asking whether to accept that exact revision. The reviewed
    pre-acceptance authoritative .think SHA-256 was
    811c9beff686909ebac00233aaf47b4f9149cd96c55ce4541a337de5220f20d4.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, D3, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    Accept exact ADR-0036 revision 1 as a supplement to Accepted ADR-0034.
    This acceptance does not itself authorize selector implementation, Seal
    promotion, commit, push, deployment, or cc304 completion.
